> Registration
> ------------
>=20
> Not many people registered up to now. Please register as soon as possible=
 if you did not do so yet, so that I have a feeling who actually will come.=
 If you registered for the LF Summit and did not mention that you want to a=
ttend the OpenPrinting Summit, please post here. Post here also if you regi=
stered for the LF Summit and got rejected by the organization team of the L=
F Summit.
>=20
>=20
> Participation by Phone
> ----------------------
>=20
> If you will participate by call-in, please post here. So I know who I can=
 expect to call in. If you call in only for a part of the session, please t=
ell to which sessions. You are not required by that to call in only on the =
specified sessions. You can call in whenever you like. The conference phone=
s are set up during the whole meeting.
>=20
> Note that AFAIK call-in participation is only available for the OpenPrint=
ing Summit, not the other sessions of the LF Collaboration Summit.
>=20
>=20
> Presentations
> -------------
>=20
> Please post here if you want to give a presentation. Upload your=20
> presentation as PDF file to the OpenPrinting Summit web site and link=20
> it from the appropriate session in the agenda.
>=20
> It would be great to do this until March 31 so that we can talk about=20
> it on the planning conference call. Please upload the presentation=20
> until April 3 at the latest to give the atendees some preparation time=20
> for the discussion. You can re-upload if you have updates.
>=20
> Do not hesitate to give a presentation when you only participate by=20
> call-in. We will show your slides while you are talking on the phone.
> This worked great with Mike Sweet's presentation on the Printing=20
> Summit in Lexington in 2006.
